# FurryOS desktop package list (injected into live-build chroot)
# KDE Plasma desktop + SDDM display manager + FurryOS branding prerequisites

## Core desktop
kde-plasma-desktop
plasma-workspace
plasma-desktop
sddm
sddm-theme-breeze

## KDE applications and settings
systemsettings
konsole
dolphin
kde-config-sddm
kinfocenter

## Look and feel infrastructure (note: plasma-look-and-feel is NOT shipped in
## Ubuntu noble's archive; the Breeze global theme + color-schemes provide the
## look-and-feel layer instead)
##
## NOTE: there is no package literally named "color-schemes" in Ubuntu noble -
## that is a Debian-ism. On noble the Breeze colour schemes
## (/usr/share/color-schemes/Breeze*.colors) are shipped by kde-style-breeze,
## which is already listed below. Verified against the noble package index:
##   kde-style-breeze_5.27.11-0ubuntu3 -> ./usr/share/color-schemes/Breeze{Light,Dark,Classic}.colors
breeze
breeze-icon-theme
kde-style-breeze

## Fonts and rendering
fonts-noto-color-emoji
fontconfig

## Base tooling needed for branding hooks and verification
ca-certificates
curl
wget
less
sudo
locales
console-setup
kbd

## Network (SSH login banner verification requirement)
openssh-server
openssh-client

## SDDM theme QML runtime dependencies (reported by sddm-experience, t3)
##
## The FurryOS login theme is pure QtQuick 2 + QtQml + QtQuick.Layouts and
## does NOT use org.kde.plasma.* or SddmComponents, so these are the only
## real runtime requirements beyond the `sddm` package itself:
##
##   qml-module-qtquick2 / libqt5quick5  - without them the whole theme fails
##                                        to load and SDDM silently falls back
##                                        to the default theme
##   qml-module-qtquick-layouts          - Main.qml uses RowLayout/ColumnLayout
##   qt5-image-formats                   - provides libqsvg.so. The paw print is
##                                        an SVG; WITHOUT this package the paw
##                                        silently disappears (no error), which
##                                        is the hardest failure to diagnose.
##
## On noble most of these are pulled in as dependencies of sddm / kde-plasma-
## desktop, but they are declared explicitly so the failure mode above can
## never be introduced by a dependency change.
##
## NOTE on naming: on noble the SVG image-format plugin lives in
## qt5-image-formats-plugins. There is NO binary package called
## "qt5-image-formats" in the noble index any more (that name only exists as
## a source package), so only the -plugins name is listed. Verified:
##   grep '^Package: qt5-image-formats-plugins$' in the noble universe index
qml-module-qtquick2
qml-module-qtquick-layouts
libqt5quick5
qt5-image-formats-plugins
